# ALL.mask -- line masks for uni_cs410 (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason), read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar().
*	PART:^Base time at entry was +([0-9]+) seconds and ([0-9]+) microsecomds$	the program prints the clock (gettimeofday, timefuncs.icn) and never tests it: a clock reading, never the answer, masked on both sides as a system variance (Lon 2026-11-13: "remember we have the masking feature for system/runtime variances that are correct but otherwise different."); MEASURED: two runs a second apart differ in these lines alone (a PART mask since 2026-11-18, row unicon-every-no-oracle-answer-exclusion-is-measured-again-and-cut-or-says-why: gameFinal's four-line answer holds two clock lines, and a whole-line mask would cover half of it; the part mask takes the two numbers and keeps the words)
*	PART:^Time passed since entry is ([0-9]+) seconds and ([0-9]+) microsecomds$	the program prints the clock (gettimeofday, timefuncs.icn) and never tests it: a clock reading, never the answer, masked on both sides as a system variance (Lon 2026-11-13: "remember we have the masking feature for system/runtime variances that are correct but otherwise different."); MEASURED: two runs a second apart differ in these lines alone (a PART mask since 2026-11-18, same row: the two numbers masked, the words graded)
